","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-11T21:12:45Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T08:47:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4.1.stable.mono.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 22.04 v4.4.1.stable.mono.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen unchecking \"Editable children\" for imported scene with some nested nodes hidden (while it was editable), hidden nodes are not shown again, however this state is not saved anywhere, and they are shown once the scene is reopened.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n - Add some scene with child nodes to another scene.\n - Check \"Editable children\" for the inserted scene.\n - Hide some child node in the inserted scene.\n - Uncheck \"Editable children\" for the inserted scene.\n\nDespite the warning about all changes will be lost, the node which was hidden still remains hidden, until the scene is reopened.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tmp-godot-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20698167/tmp-godot-project.zip)\n\nOpen \"main\" scene, and hide some child node in the \"inserted\" scene there after checking \"editable children\" for it. Then uncheck \"editable children\", hidden subnodes remain hidden. ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107425/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107425/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}